    "q-19276": {
      "dom_id": "step-q19276",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251721/assets/9dfaf74a497a2fd22428e09a4c26d573e184c9728ccf67f11ebb9d6a2a44f4c6.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $q+r?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we have to find $q+r.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $q+r$ goes from the tail of $q$ to the head of $r:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251721/assets/63a95b27b2255ff8d784c1d0715f4a6bf306fb4652c438288a8c404726bac83c.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=1.5=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $BH=4.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|q+r| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $q+r$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{2}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|q+r|}\\cdot (q+r) \\\\  & =\\frac{2(q+r)}{\\sqrt{73}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-19276-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{2q}{\\sqrt{13}}+\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{29}}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"70\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mrow><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D42A TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-mrow></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-msqrt><mjx-sqrt><mjx-surd><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c221A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-surd><mjx-box style=\"padding-top: 0.163em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-box></mjx-sqrt></mjx-msqrt></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle space=\"3\"><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D42B TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-msqrt><mjx-sqrt><mjx-surd><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c221A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-surd><mjx-box style=\"padding-top: 0.163em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c39\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-box></mjx-sqrt></mjx-msqrt></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">q</mi></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">r</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>29</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-19276-b",
